        {
          "type": "application",
          "title": "How to Read Along With This Course",
          "content": "You can take this course without reading the novel, but if you do read it, here is a way to get the most out of both.\n\n**Keep a two-column notebook.** In one column, note what Rand wants you to admire. In the other, note where you resist -- where a character seems unreal, a speech seems preachy, or a moral judgment seems too harsh. Both columns are evidence.\n\n**Ask three questions of every major character:**\n• Where does this person get their sense of worth?\n• What do they want from other people?\n• What would they do if no one were watching?\n\n**Discussion starter:** Think of someone you know -- or yourself -- who changed a decision because of what others would think. Was that weakness, as Rand would argue, or ordinary social wisdom? Hold onto your answer. By Lesson 12 you will be able to test it against Rand's argument and her critics' replies.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">YOUR READING TOOLKIT</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Three questions for every character</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"180\" width=\"800\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"245\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">1.</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"245\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Where does their sense of worth come from?</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"320\" width=\"800\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"385\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">2.</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"385\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">What do they want from other people?</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"460\" width=\"800\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"525\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">3.</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"525\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">What would they do if no one watched?</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"640\" width=\"460\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.1)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"720\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">ADMIRE</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"770\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">What Rand wants you to</text><rect x=\"580\" y=\"640\" width=\"460\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"720\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">RESIST</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"770\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Where you push back</text></svg>",
            "caption": "A notebook method and three character questions for reading The Fountainhead critically."
          }
        }
