        {
          "type": "application",
          "title": "Drill: Steelman, Then Critique",
          "content": "Practice arguing about Roark fairly. Take one of his key decisions -- **refusing the bank's classical facade** -- and work through it in three steps.\n\n**1. Steelman.** Make the strongest case for Roark. Consider: a building lasts a century; a design is a unified idea; a facade that contradicts the structure is a lie told to every passerby; if he bends once, why not always?\n\n**2. Critique.** Now make the strongest case against. Consider: the bank is paying; its customers' comfort is a legitimate goal; a skilled architect might find a design that honors both; closing his office helps no one.\n\n**3. Decide and qualify.** Where do you land -- and under what conditions would you change your mind?\n\n**Transfer it:** Think of a time you were asked to change your work to please someone. Did you compromise, refuse, or find a third option? Rand would say the third option is usually the first compromise. Do you agree?",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">STEELMAN, THEN CRITIQUE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"23\">Case study: the bank facade</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"180\" width=\"800\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"245\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">1. STEELMAN</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"295\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">A facade that contradicts the building is a lie</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"390\" width=\"800\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"455\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">2. CRITIQUE</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"505\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Clients have legitimate needs too</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"600\" width=\"800\" height=\"170\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"665\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">3. DECIDE AND QUALIFY</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"715\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Where do you land, and what would change it?</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"840\" width=\"700\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">Is a third option a compromise?</text></svg>",
            "caption": "A three-step drill for arguing about Roark's choices fairly."
          }
        }
